I can't reproduce the page's example verbatim, because that would exceed the 125-character limit on quoted material. Here's an equivalent minimal stateless server written from the page's description:

```ts
import { McpServer } from "@modelcontextprotocol/server";
import { createMcpHandler } from "agents/mcp/server";
import { z } from "zod";

// Pass a factory, not a server instance: "Pass the factory itself."
function createServer() {
	const server = new McpServer({ name: "echo-server", version: "1.0.0" });

	server.registerTool(
		"echo",
		{
			description: "Echo back a message",
			inputSchema: { message: z.string() },
		},
		async ({ message }) => ({
			content: [{ type: "text", text: message }],
		}),
	);

	return server;
}

export default {
	fetch(request, env, ctx) {
		return createMcpHandler(createServer)(request, env, ctx);
	},
} satisfies ExportedHandler;
```

The example uses the SDK v2 `McpServer` from `@modelcontextprotocol/server`, `createMcpHandler` from `agents/mcp/server`, and `zod` for the input schema. Install them with `@modelcontextprotocol/server@2.0.0` pinned, as the page recommends. For the exact original snippet, see the MCP handler APIs page on developers.cloudflare.com.

