content.text:
Install `agents`, `@modelcontextprotocol/server` (pinned to the exact version your `agents` release expects) and `zod`. Then pass a **factory function** that builds a new v2 `McpServer` to `createMcpHandler` from `agents/mcp/server`, and call the handler from your Worker's `fetch`. Pass the function itself, not a server you've already created: the handler calls it on every request so each request gets its own server. The handler is stateless by default and still accepts older clients.

```ts
import { McpServer } from "@modelcontextprotocol/server";
import { createMcpHandler } from "agents/mcp/server";
import { z } from "zod";

function createServer() {
  const server = new McpServer({ name: "echo-server", version: "1.0.0" });
  server.registerTool("echo",
    { description: "Echo back a message", inputSchema: { message: z.string() } },
    async ({ message }) => ({ content: [{ type: "text", text: message }] }));
  return server;
}

export default {
  fetch: (req, env, ctx) => createMcpHandler(createServer)(req, env, ctx),
} satisfies ExportedHandler;
```

This needs `agents` v0.20.0 or later, which is where v2 support was added. The v0.20.0 release notes pin `@modelcontextprotocol/server@2.0.0-beta.5`, but the docs say `2.0.0`, so check which version your installed release asks for. `McpAgent` is deprecated and frozen. `createLegacyMcpHandler` is only meant as a temporary bridge for old SDK v1 endpoints. I based the example on the docs' description rather than copying the official snippet word for word.

Sources:
- [MCP handler API](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/model-context-protocol/apis/handler-api/)
- [Changelog: Agents SDK v0.20.0 / MCP SDK v2](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-07-27-agents-sdk-v0.20.0-mcp-sdk-v2/)
- [Migrate to MCP SDK v2](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/model-context-protocol/guides/migrate-to-mcp-sdk-v2/)
- [agents@0.20.0 release notes](https://newreleases.io/project/github/cloudflare/agents/release/agents@0.20.0)

